# The test at the door of a copy buys a narrower type for the price of a look at a tag. A number that lies raw in a register has no tag: "a fraction" is three instructions, "an int32 or a fraction" thirty,
# in every turn, and what they buy is the knowledge of which numbers a double is. The copy is walked with the type that the argument has: the element goes from its read into the sum.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: [[element]]: number @Double = GetArrayElement {{*}}arrayStorage=Double level=Proven {{*}}isPresent
# CHECK-NOT: = TypeTest [[element]]
# CHECK-NOT: = Narrowed [[element]]
# CHECK: = Add {{*}}, [[element]] form=Numbers
